          m_Value: 1
        m_EnumType:
          m_Identification: BookGraph.Runtime.PageEffect, Assembly-CSharp, Version=0.0.0.0,
            Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null
    - rid: 8910043418339312017
      type: {class: 'Constant`1[[System.Int32, mscorlib]]', ns: Unity.GraphToolkit.Editor, asm: Unity.GraphToolkit.Internal.Editor}
      data:
        m_Value: 13
    - rid: 8910043418339312018
      type: {class: 'Constant`1[[System.String, mscorlib]]', ns: Unity.GraphToolkit.Editor, asm: Unity.GraphToolkit.Internal.Editor}
      data:
        m_Value: There is one thing that drives me to doubt this theory though. We
          had a sample of five people, one of which contracted this infection, we
          had immediately quarantined the rest, keeping them under watch as we expected
          that they would show signs of this sickness soon enough. Yet none of them
          contracted it. A week later we quarantined a group of six expecting that
          they would follow a similar pattern, four of them contracted it while the
          other two showed no signs. We are short on man power, the bodies are piling
          up as I write, I do not know how long we can maintain this. May the Veil
          guide us.
    - rid: 8910043418339312019
      type: {class: DefaultPage, ns: BookGraph.Editor, asm: Assembly-CSharp-Editor}
      data: 
